  "query_preview": "..\nThe forecast remains in good shape. Isolated trade-wind showers are\nto be expected through at least the beginning of next week. This\nshould be considered the first taste of the dry season. So far this \nmonth we have had 0.40 inches of rain, about 2.28 inches lower than\nthe average so far for November. While the Marianas are not yet in\ndrought conditions, drought conditions may be anticipated later this\ndry season. For now, fairer weather days are expected, but try to \nstart conserving water as we are transitioning into the dry season.",
